cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "rafkit: autocatalytic (RAF) sets in catalytic reaction networks"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: James P.
    family-names: Galasyn
  - given-names: Claude
    family-names: Théodore
repository-code: "https://github.com/JimGalasyn/rafkit"
url: "https://github.com/JimGalasyn/rafkit"
abstract: >-
  A dependency-light Python implementation of RAF theory (Hordijk & Steel 2004):
  maximal RAFs, the strictly autocatalytic variant, irreducible-RAF sampling and
  census, exploitability, and Kauffman's binary polymer model with optional
  cleavage. Every algorithm carries hand-computed known-answer tests, and the
  suite additionally checks maximal-RAF and strictly-autocatalytic results against
  counts produced by CatReNet, the reference implementation, on a committed
  fixture — so an independent implementation validates this one on every run with
  no Java required. Reads and writes CatReNet's CRS interchange format.
keywords:
